[THOUGHT] The available lab results (CBC, glucose, creatinine, electrolytes) are normal — reassuring for common metabolic causes, but critical tests remain pending: TSH, B12/folate, syphilis serology, HIV, and especially brain MRI. These are indispensable to exclude endocrine, nutritional, infectious, or structural etiologies. Since the Medical Analyst’s reply only listed *some* results and marked others as “Not specified”, I must now explicitly request the *missing* high-yield labs and the MRI — but per protocol, I can only request *one* test per turn. The MRI is the single most discriminating test here: frontal/temporal atrophy would strongly support bvFTD; normal imaging would prompt urgent reconsideration of psychiatric, toxic, or inflammatory mimics. So I prioritize the MRI result.

[TEST] Brain MRI with contrast — report on:  
- Volume loss in frontal and anterior temporal lobes (especially orbitofrontal and dorsolateral prefrontal cortex);  
- Presence of T2/FLAIR hyperintensities, white matter lesions, or signal abnormalities;  
- Midbrain or basal ganglia involvement;  
- Any mass lesion or vascular abnormality.

